diagnostics/operators-shadowed-trait.em:4:7: warning: `Ordered` hides Emerald's built-in `Ordered`
  trait Ordered {
        ^^^^^^^
A name the program declares always wins, so `Ordered` here means this one. Write `Emerald.Ordered` to reach the built-in, or choose a different name.
diagnostics/operators-shadowed-trait.em:17:7: `<` needs Card to adopt the prelude's `Ordered`
  print(Card(1) < Card(2))
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
This program declares its own `Ordered`, which takes the prelude's place wherever the name is written, but operators run only through the prelude's. Adopt the built-in as `with Emerald.Ordered`, or rename this program's `Ordered`.
